        "license": "CC BY-SA4.0; viewed only",
        "observations": "Actually inspected full ordinary photograph: seven plain pink/red shafts with white moulded bases above broad pale steps, low brick rectangles, eroded isolated concrete wall cores, scattered round drums and a long fallen shaft on pale paving. Later church and neighboring Forum remain independent. No pixels copied."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2016_Temple_of_Peace_(Rome)_03.jpg",
        "author": "Jordiferrer",
        "date": "2016-08-04",
        "license": "CC BY-SA4.0; viewed only",
        "observations": "Actually inspected complementary wide view: plain shafts with broken flat tops, broad continuous steps, long low rectangular court traces, piles of separated pink drums and pale paving strips. The exposed remains have no restored temple roof or entablature. Later background churches are context, not part of this asset."
      }
